# Trivy vulnerability exceptions (spec 006 / T002, FR-002).
#
# Only upstream-UNFIXABLE findings may be listed here, each as an explicit,
# justified, time-bounded exception. Never add a fixable CVE to silence the
# gate, and never lower the gate severity — remediate at the dependency/base
# image instead. The image-scan gate runs with `ignore-unfixed: true`, so
# unfixed findings do not block; entries here document accepted risk for audit.
#
# Format:
#   CVE-XXXX-YYYYY  # <justification> — review-by: YYYY-MM-DD
#
# auth-api currently has ZERO exceptions: the migration to Go modules,
# golang-jwt/jwt v5, Echo v4, and bumped x/crypto/x/net/x/text/grpc cleared all
# HIGH/CRITICAL findings (fixable and unfixed). Keep this file empty of CVEs.
